> Welcome! In this module, you will learn the small pieces that make every C program possible.

## 🎯 Learning objectives

By the end of this module, you will be able to:

- Explain what C tokens are and why they are important
- Identify identifiers, keywords, constants, string literals, operators, and special symbols
- Distinguish valid and invalid identifiers
- Use operators and symbols to construct C expressions
- Recognize the structure of a basic C program

## 🎁 What you will gain

After completing this module, you will be able to:

- Break down C statements into smaller meaningful parts
- Understand how the compiler reads your source code
- Spot syntax errors more quickly
- Read C code with more confidence
- Build a strong base before learning variables, loops, and functions

